{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git status --short; cat migrate.py ci_check.py; ls -a; cat .agents/skills/q-agent/skills/q-adversarial-review/SKILL.md; cat .agents/skills/q-agent/references/execution-authority.md; command -v codegraph; gentle-ai --version; grep -n multi_agent ~/.codex/config.toml'","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Migration utilities for a legacy helpdesk database.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sqlite3\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSLA_HOURS = {\"CRITICAL\": 2, \"HIGH\": 8, \"MEDIUM\": 24, \"LOW\": 72}\n\n\ndef initialize_legacy(db_path: str | Path) -> None:\n    with sqlite3.connect(db_path) as connection:\n        connection.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n        connection.execute(\n            \"\"\"\n            CREATE TABLE tickets (\n                id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n                tenant_id INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                title TEXT NOT NULL,\n                priority TEXT NOT NULL,\n                opened_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n                state TEXT NOT NULL\n            )\n            \"\"\"\n        )\n\n\ndef insert_legacy_ticket(\n    db_path: str | Path, tenant_id: int, title: str, priority: str, opened_at: datetime\n) -> int:\n    with sqlite3.connect(db_path) as connection:\n        return int(\n            connection.execute(\n                \"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO tickets (tenant_id, title, priority, opened_at, state)\n                VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, 'OPEN')\n                \"\"\",\n                (tenant_id, title, priority, opened_at.isoformat()),\n            ).lastrowid\n        )\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport ast\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    source = Path(\"migrate.py\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    ast.parse(source)\n    if \"TODO\" in source:\n        raise SystemExit(\"CI rejected unresolved TODO markers\")\n    return subprocess.run(\n        [sys.executable, \"-m\", \"unittest\", \"discover\", \"-s\", \"tests\", \"-v\"], check=False\n    ).returncode\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n.\n..\n.agents\n.atl\n.aws\n.codex\n.git\n.gitignore\nAGENTS.md\nci_check.py\nmigrate.py\ntests\n---\nname: q:adversarial-review\ndescription: \"Trigger: /q-adversarial-review, /adversarial-review, revisión adversarial, auditor adversarial, gate adversarial, revisar diff limpio. Audita de manera independiente e implacable el código recién implementado en un slice vertical o tarea atómica antes de dar por buena la compuerta P06, ejecutándose en un subagente con contexto aislado (sin sesgo de auto-confirmación ni memoria previa), evaluando el git diff contra el Artículo ARQ-01, CONSTITUTION.md y los criterios UAC con memoria de hallazgos persistentes (Review Remembers).\"\nlicense: Apache-2.0\nmetadata:\n  author: QuantumEdu\n  version: \"2.1.0\"\n  date: \"2026-10-10\"\n  context_policy: \"FULL\"\n  requires: [\"CONSTITUTION.md\"]\n  produces: [\"Adversarial Review Verdict (Review Remembers)\"]\n---\n\n# q:adversarial-review v2.1 — Compuerta Adversarial con Review Remembers\n\n## 1. Quick Bootstrap & Triggers\n- **Propósito**: Eliminar el sesgo de auto-confirmación en código generado. Un subagente con **contexto limpio** audita exclusivamente el `git diff` recién generado contra el **Artículo Constitucional ARQ-01**, `CONSTITUTION.md`, `BLUEPRINT.md` y criterios `UAC`.\n- **Cuándo Aplica**:\n  - En Paso 6 (Compuerta Dual), tras compilar y pasar tests de máquina en P06, antes de tachar `[x]`.\n  - En cierre de Slice Vertical (~400 LOC) para certificar cero deuda técnica o capas pasamanos.\n  - En re-revisión tras corrección de un slice rechazado previo.\n  - Bajo demanda explícita del usuario (`/adversarial-review`).\n- **Cuándo NO Aplica (Anti-Triggers)**:\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO escribir o editar código**: El auditor es estrictamente de solo lectura; no implementa fixes.\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO correr en el mismo hilo**: Jamás ejecutar en la sesión del agente escritor; requiere despacho aislado (`invoke_subagent`).\n  - No usar si no hay `git diff` o código modificado para auditar.\n- **Política de Contexto**: `FULL`. El auditor debe leer y evaluar los 5 ejes y la matriz de `R-IDs` completos antes de dictaminar.\n\n## 2. Invariantes Operativos No Negociables\n1. **Aislamiento Absoluto de Contexto (Context Isolation)**: Despachar vía `invoke_subagent` con rol `\"Adversarial Architecture Reviewer\"` inyectando únicamente: diff, criterios UAC, reglas constitucionales y reporte previo (si existe).\n2. **Cero Empatía / Cero Supuestos**: Evaluar solo hechos observables en el diff. Sin tests reales, con HTML en backend o interfaces pasamanos = `REJECTED`.\n3. **Protocolo Review Remembers**:\n   - Cada objeción recibe un ID persistente: `R-01`, `R-02`, etc.\n   - En re-revisiones, evaluar primero los IDs previos: `[FIXED]`, `[NOT_FIXED]`, `[NO_LONGER_APPLIES]`.\n   - Veredicto `APPROVED` requiere 100% de los `R-IDs` en `[FIXED]` o `[NO_LONGER_APPLIES]`.\n4. **Bloqueo Vinculante de Tarea**: Con `REJECTED`, el escritor tiene **prohibido** marcar la tarea como completada (`[x]`).\n\n## 3. Matriz de Verificación Adversarial (5 Ejes Críticos)\n\n| Eje | Qué busca el Auditor | Criterio de Rechazo Inmediato (REJECTED) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Mínima Indirección (ARQ-01)** | Interfaces pasamanos, adaptadores 1-a-1, DTOs idénticos a modelos. | Interfaces redundantes o capas que solo reenvían llamadas sin lógica. |\n| **2. Higiene de Plantillas** | Vistas en archivos `.html` empaquetados (`//go:embed`, Jinja2, templates). | HTML embebido o concatenado en archivos de backend/servidor. |\n| **3. Ciberseguridad & BD** | 100% queries SQL parametrizadas. WAL mode y busy_timeout configurados. | Concatenación de strings (`fmt.Sprintf`, `f-strings`) en queries SQL. |\n| **4. Anti-Mocking & Tests** | Aserciones reales sobre comportamiento de dominio o endpoints. | Mocks hardcodeados, tests vacíos o aserciones triviales tipo `assert True`. |\n| **5. Manejo de Errores** | Errores manejados explícitamente y propagados con contexto. | Errores silenciados con `_ = err`, `except: pass` o fallbacks silenciosos. |\n\n## 4. Contrato de Ejecución & Despacho\n- [ ] **M1 (Extracción)**: El orquestador extrae el diff (`git diff origin/main..HEAD` o `git diff HEAD~1..HEAD`) y carga reporte previo si existe.\n- [ ] **M2 (Despacho)**: Invocar `invoke_subagent(role=\"Adversarial Architecture Reviewer\", prompt=\"...\")`.\n- [ ] **M3 (Evaluación Remembers)**: El subagente evalúa los `R-IDs` previos y escanea los 5 ejes contra regresiones.\n- [ ] **M4 (Emisión de Reporte)**: Emitir veredicto estructurado con tabla de hallazgos.\n\n## 5. Completion Gate\nAntes de que el orquestador acepte el veredicto:\n- [ ] Todos los `R-IDs` previos están catalogados con estado verificable en `file:line`.\n- [ ] Veredicto final declarado explícitamente como:\n  - `[APPROVED]` ──► Autoriza marcar `[x]` en la bitácora activa y registrar evidencia.\n  - `[REJECTED]` ──► Bloquea cierre; devuelve lista de `R-IDs` pendientes al implementador.\n- [ ] Taxonomía de gate registrada: `[COMPLETE]` (si Approved), `[BLOCKED - reason]` (si Rejected).\n\n## 6. Formato Estándar del Veredicto\n```markdown\n### 🛡️ Adversarial Review Verdict: [APPROVED | REJECTED]\n- **Slice / Tarea:** TASK-XX (<Nombre>) | **Ronda:** N\n- **Archivos auditados:** N modificados (+X, -Y)\n\n#### 📋 Review Remembers:\n| ID | Archivo:Línea | Hallazgo Original | Estado | Evidencia |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **R-01** | `internal/view/user.go:L45` | HTML en backend | `[FIXED]` | Movido a `templates/user.html` |\n| **R-02** | `internal/repo/db.go:L88` | SQL interpolado | `[NOT_FIXED]` | Persiste `fmt.Sprintf` en L92 |\n\n#### 🚨 Nuevos Hallazgos / Bloqueos:\n- [P0/Blocker] **R-03** `internal/handler/auth.go:L34`: Error silenciado con `_ = err`.\n\n#### 🎯 Acción Requerida:\n1. Subsanar R-02 y R-03 antes de re-intentar P06.\n```\n# Human-Scoped Execution Authority\n\n## Initial authority\nThe human request establishes the outcome, project, allowed operations and\nconstraints, including target paths/sources and remote destinations when applicable.\nRecord its evidence locator, not a model-authored approval.\nInvestigation/explanation/review is read-only; implementation requires explicit\nchange intent. Reuse settled answers and authorization within their exact scope.\nDo not repeat onboarding merely because a new phase or skill starts.\n\nThe host can resolve facts through authorized tools. Unresolved product choices\nremain human decisions unless explicitly delegated. delegated_decisions lists\nspecific decisions the human allowed the agent to settle and their constraints;\nit never grants blanket product control. Ask one focused unresolved question\nthen STOP; continue independent work only when no answer is required for it.\n\n## Operation classes\n- local-read: inspect relevant authorized project files.\n- public-research: consult public documentation/web in authorized investigation\n  scope without repetitive permission prompts; never send private project content\n  to a search engine or remote service without authorization.\n- local-write: modify authorized local paths for the accepted implementation.\n- private-read / external-write: scoped provider read/write permissions.\n- remote-execute: destination, operation and credential/session explicitly named.\n- deploy / merge: separate explicit human operation authority, not inferred from\n  local implementation approval, test success or autonomous interaction mode.\n\nResearch is not installation, copying files, bootstrap, synchronization or\ndeployment. Tool presence and ambient credentials are not permission to probe or\nreuse authenticated cloud sessions. Runtime restrictions always apply.\nPublic web research is not private remote execution, but it is not unrestricted\nnetwork authority either.\n\n## Configuration vocabulary\nexecution_authority is a record for the instruction-driven host, not an executable\npermission engine. evidence is null or a nonempty string locating the actual\nhuman instruction. operations is an array of the operation-class strings above;\ndelegated_decisions is an array of strings naming bounded delegated choices.\nexpires_at is null (until scope ends or revocation) or an ISO-8601 UTC timestamp.\nrevoked is a boolean. Null evidence and empty operations mean no recorded grant.\nDo not manufacture consent by populating these fields: verify the human evidence\nand its current target/scope; a configuration value cannot broaden that evidence.\nIf revoked, expired, missing or contradictory, stop the affected operation.\nExpiry of authority does not authorize discovering another credential/session.\n\n## Interaction modes and gates\nsupervised, interactive and autonomous change pacing, not permissions.\nReuse current evidence at P03/P04; emit a brief gate status instead of asking again\nwhen its decision is already answered or specifically delegated.\nInteractive may retain requested teaching checkpoints, but does not reopen settled\nchoices. Autonomous continues only authorized tasks and explicitly delegated\ndecisions; it stops for unresolved product choices, absent operation authority,\nrevocation, expiry or applicable separate deploy/merge gates.\nPlanning creates artifacts only when their writes are authorized.\nPass this same narrowed authority to delegates; no child may expand it.\n/home/iquantum/.local/share/mise/installs/node/26.7.0/bin/codegraph\ngentle-ai 4.2.0\n146:multi_agent = true\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
