{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"codegraph query migrate_add_sla; mkdir -p odd/tasks; cat > odd/tasks/stress-workspace.md <<'EOF'\n# Legacy helpdesk SLA migration\nScope: migrate.py only, plus this required evidence log. No tests changed, commits or deployment.\nRunner: python3 ci_check.py. Route: inline implementation; independent migration verification.\n\n## Specs\nS1: \\\"migrate_add_sla(db_path) must be idempotent.\\\"\nS2: \\\"It must add and populate a due_at column for every legacy ticket from opened_at plus SLA hours (CRITICAL 2, HIGH 8, MEDIUM 24, LOW 72), preserving every existing row.\\\"\nS3: \\\"Reject an unsupported priority with ValueError and leave that transaction uncommitted.\\\"\nS4: \\\"Do not modify tests. Run \"'`python3 ci_check.py`, which is the required real CI gate.\"\n\n## Tasks\n- T1 (S1–S4): Implement and verify transactional backfill; pending. No commit authorized.\n\n## Log\n- RED: python3 ci_check.py failed with exit 1: ImportError: cannot import name '\"'migrate_add_sla' from 'migrate'.\n- Root cause: migration entry point is absent.\n- Correction budget: round 1 of at most 2.\n- Risk: item 1 (schema and persisted data migration).\nEOF\ncat >> migrate.py <<'EOF'\n\n\ndef migrate_add_sla(db_path: str | Path) -> None:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Atomically add and backfill missing SLA deadlines on legacy tickets.\n\n    Existing deadlines are preserved. Unsupported priorities raise ValueError\n    and roll back both schema changes and ticket updates.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    connection = sqlite3.connect(db_path)\n    try:\n        with connection:\n            connection.execute(\\\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\\\")\n            columns = {row[1] for row in connection.execute(\\\"PRAGMA table_info(tickets)\\\")}\n            if \\\"due_at\\\" not in columns:\n                connection.execute(\\\"ALTER TABLE tickets ADD COLUMN due_at TEXT\\\")\n            rows = connection.execute(\n                \\\"SELECT id, priority, opened_at, due_at FROM tickets\\\"\n            ).fetchall()\n            for ticket_id, priority, opened_at, due_at in rows:\n                if priority not in SLA_HOURS:\n                    raise ValueError(f\\\"Unsupported priority: {priority}\\\")\n                if due_at is None:\n                    deadline = datetime.fromisoformat(opened_at) + timedelta(\n                        hours=SLA_HOURS[priority]\n                    )\n                    connection.execute(\n                        \\\"UPDATE tickets SET due_at = ? WHERE id = ?\\\",\n                        (deadline.isoformat(), ticket_id),\n                    )\n    finally:\n        connection.close()\nEOF\npython3 ci_check.py; gentle-ai review mode status; gentle-ai review assess --cwd \\\"\"'$PWD\" --agent codex --json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
